      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Recognize Ollama WorkOS session cookies",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add the WorkOS AuthKit `wos-session` cookie to the Ollama session-cookie allowlist\n- recognize `wos-session` in both the manual cookie-header resolver and the imported-browser-cookie selector\n- keep legacy Ollama / NextAuth / `__Secure-session` cookie names working\n\n## Live runtime proof\n\nA live probe linked against `CodexBarCore` drove the real `OllamaUsageFetcher` against `https://ollama.com/settings` with a synthetic (invalid) `wos-session` cookie and a redirect logger. No real account or secret was used:\n\n```text\n$ swift test --disable-sandbox --filter LiveOllamaWorkOSProbe\nresolveManualCookieHeader accepted wos-session: true\nresolved header: wos-session=probe-invalid-session; theme=dark\nselectSessionInfo accepted wos-session-only: true\n[ollama] Using manual cookie header\n[ollama] Cookie names: wos-session, theme\n[ollama] Redirect 303 https://ollama.com/settings -> https://ollama.com/signin\n[ollama] Redirect 303 https://ollama.com/signin -> https://api.workos.com/user_management/authorize?client_id=...&provider=authkit&redirect_uri=...&response_type=code\n[ollama] Redirect 302 https://api.workos.com/user_management/authorize?... -> https://signin.ollama.com/?client_id=...&authorization_session_id=01KWWXY00VJ6BR3RW21VXK03C3\n[ollama] Response: 200 https://signin.ollama.com/?client_id=...\n[ollama] Parse failed: Could not parse Ollama usage: Missing Ollama usage data.\nRESULT: fetch threw -> parseFailed(\"Missing Ollama usage data.\")\n✔ Test run with 1 test in 1 suite passed after 1.755 seconds.\n```\n\nOn `main`, the same probe throws `noSessionCookie` from `resolveManualCookieHeader` and the imported-cookie selector rejects a `wos-session`-only session, because the allowlist omits that name. With this branch, `wos-session` is recognized in both the manual-header path and the browser-import selector, and the real fetcher sends it against `ollama.com` (the captured redirect chain above is the live Ollama/WorkOS sign-in flow).\n\nThe cookie is synthetic and invalid, so the live endpoint (correctly) does not authenticate; the proof target is cookie-name recognition and the real fetch path, not a successful usage read.\n\n## Note for the maintainer\nThe real Ollama WorkOS sign-in flow (captured live above) uses `api.workos.com/user_management/authorize` as an intermediate hop and lands on `signin.ollama.com`. The `wos-session` cookie is the session name WorkOS AuthKit issues after a successful sign-in; recognizing it lets CodexBar import a real WorkOS-authenticated browser session instead of only legacy NextAuth/Ollama session names. No live authenticated account was available to capture a successful usage read, so the success path remains covered by the focused injected-transport tests (the selector and resolver accept `wos-session`; existing tests cover the parse path).\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests` (21 passed, incl. new `manual mode accepts workos session cookie header` and `cookie selector accepts workos session cookie`)\n- live probe above against the real `ollama.com` / WorkOS sign-in flow (1.76s)\n- `swift build` clean",
        "branch": "fix/ollama-authjs-cookies",
